Feature: Hand launch
  The plane starts in your hand. To throw it, hold the throttle above 55 %, as you do at the
  field. You can also press Space. R picks the plane up again: the sim carries it back to
  your hand, and then you can throw it again. [[Your first throw]] shows each step.

  Expectation: Throttle up throws the plane
    This is the launch that you use at the field. Hold the throttle above 55 % for a short
    time, and the plane goes.
    Given the plane is in hand
    When the throttle is above 55 %
    Then the plane is flying

  Expectation: Space throws the plane
    Space throws the plane at the throttle that you set. Use it when you fly with the
    throttle low, or when the sim waits for a throw in AUTO.
    Given the plane is in hand
    And the sim is running
    When the pilot throws the plane
    Then the plane is flying

  Expectation: Reset picks the plane back up
    Close the throttle first. If the throttle is open, the plane goes again when it is back
    in your hand. While the sim carries the plane back, the HUD says "Bringing it back to
    your hand...".
    Given the throttle is below 55 %
    When the pilot resets the plane
    Then the plane is in hand

  Expectation: A throw with the nose down crashes the plane
    If you hold the stick forward, the plane flies into the ground immediately after it
    leaves your hand.
    Overrides: Throttle up throws the plane
    Given the plane is in hand
    And the pitch stick is forward
    When the throttle is above 55 %
    Then the plane is crashed
